  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Caritas Asia Programme Evaluation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Caritas Asia serves as the regional coordinating office for CI member organisations operating in countries and territories in Asia. Caritas Asia has 23 member organisations that are situated in four sub-regions of Central Asia, East Asia, South Asia, and South East Asia. Caritas Asia&#x2019;s mandate is to build the institutional and human resource capacities of its member organisations. It does this through various capacity building activities under four thematic programmes (emergency/DRR; anti-trafficking; sustainable agriculture; and organisational strengthening). 

This project will provide funding for a semi-external evaluation that will review Caritas Asia&#x2019;s work, focussing on its approach to capacity building. The evaluation will assess the design, strategies, and activities of Caritas Asia&#x2019;s programmes, in order to obtain key leanings on how it can better fulfil its mandate of strengthening the capacities of its member organisations. The results and learning from the evaluation will be used to inform Caritas Asia&#x2019;s Strategic Planning in March 2015.</narrative>
  </description>
